ganW(){return"No upcoming events in the loaded calendar."},
gao9(){return"View the proposed dates."},
ganH(){return"Check the band\u2019s proposed dates."},
gZU(){return"Members"},
ganT(){return"No visible members in the project data."},
gauO(){return"How do I use Today, Calendar and Band?"},
gasu(){return"The app opens Calendar. Today shows the next event in the loaded data, two following appointments and open polls for the selected project. Notifications are in the bell. Open agenda opens Agenda for the project; Agenda in the bottom bar shows appointments across bands with search and filters. Calendar keeps the grid, Personal/Band and history: in Personal mode, choose Busy, Tentative or Free for the selected day. A check marks the current state; tapping it again makes no change. Free removes only your unavailability. For individual dates or ranges, tap + and Edit unavailability. Band shows project name, groups and members for the owner and protects unsaved edits before leaving. Other members only see data allowed by their role. The search icon at the top of Today and Calendar opens the Search events screen for the selected project, with date and history search. Agenda remains available from the bottom bar with its own search field across bands. In Agenda the search icon replaces Refresh; the notification bell and menu remain available. Pull down the list to refresh events. In the member view of Band, the panel shows the group and members visible in the already-loaded data, with their count; project management remains restricted to the owner. In the read-only Band view, members are sorted alphabetically by name, ignoring case and leading or trailing spaces."},
